      "html": "<p>This species occurs along the Pacific coast from Ecuador to Nicaragua.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/uca_ornata_en/",
      "html": "<p>Specific information on keeping this species is not yet available, but it will probably not differ substantially from that for other fiddler crabs. The aquarium should have a large land area on which the fiddler crabs preferably stay, as well as a water area with shallow water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/uca_ornata_en/",
      "html": "<p>They have no high requirements regarding food; nearly every food offered is eaten greedily.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/uca_ornata_en/",
      "html": "<p>In January 2006 the fiddler crab Uca ornata was imported to Germany for the first time. Only a few animals were obtained from Ecuador, and further imports of this species are hoped for.</p>"
    }
